What breaks: the MNT Reform 2 with the i.MX8MQ module does not work fully on a
mainline kernel (internal display, PCIe reference clock, suspend, HDMI).
Why only this target: the code this patch touches is used by the i.MX8MQ only.
Origin: MNT Research kernel tree, branch mnt-v7.3.3, commit 87301004da45
(https://source.mnt.re/reform/linux). Not in mainline.
Drop when: mainline carries the same change, or MNT drops it from its tree.

From 87301004da45c1cf5050bb851b81cd32a63e1249 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Lucie L. Hartmann" <lucie@mntre.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Sep 2022 06:20:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nwl-dsi-fixup-mode-only-for-LCDIF-input-not-DCSS

---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/nwl-dsi.c | 13 ++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/nwl-dsi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/nwl-dsi.c
index 09992529f3d8..0947c2c40d55 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/nwl-dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/nwl-dsi.c
@@ -821,10 +821,17 @@ static int nwl_dsi_bridge_atomic_check(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
 				       struct drm_connector_state *conn_state)
 {
 	struct drm_display_mode *adjusted_mode = &crtc_state->adjusted_mode;
+	struct device_node *remote;
+	struct nwl_dsi *dsi = bridge_to_dsi(bridge);
+
+	remote = of_graph_get_remote_node(dsi->dev->of_node, 0,
+						NWL_DSI_ENDPOINT_LCDIF);
 
-	/* At least LCDIF + NWL needs active high sync */
-	adjusted_mode->flags |= (DRM_MODE_FLAG_PHSYNC | DRM_MODE_FLAG_PVSYNC);
-	adjusted_mode->flags &= ~(DRM_MODE_FLAG_NHSYNC | DRM_MODE_FLAG_NVSYNC);
+	if (remote) {
+		/* At least LCDIF + NWL needs active high sync */
+		adjusted_mode->flags |= (DRM_MODE_FLAG_PHSYNC | DRM_MODE_FLAG_PVSYNC);
+		adjusted_mode->flags &= ~(DRM_MODE_FLAG_NHSYNC | DRM_MODE_FLAG_NVSYNC);
+	}
 
 	/*
 	 * Do a full modeset if crtc_state->active is changed to be true.
-- 
